  m_Name: Anemone
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FlowerData
  id: anemone
  displayName: Anemone
  scientificName: Anemone flaccida
  markerImageName: anemone
  description: "Anemone flaccida is a small, rhizomatous woodland perennial in the
    buttercup family, Ranunculaceae. It grows to around 20\u201330 cm tall and gradually
    spreads into soft colonies. Its lobed green leaves appear in spring, followed
    by delicate white, cup-shaped flowers, usually carried singly above the foliage.
    After flowering, the plant may become dormant until the following growing season."
  origin: "East Asia \u2014 primarily China and Japan"
  meaning: Anticipation, protection and gentle affection. Anemones are also sometimes
    associated with fragility and the fleeting nature of beauty because their delicate
    flowers move easily in the wind.
  habitat: Moist, shaded woodland floors, stream banks, forest margins and valleys
    with cool, humus-rich soil.
  birthflower: Not an official traditional birth flower; best associated with spring.
  floweringSeason: "April\u2013August, depending on climate and location"
  sunlight: Partial shade to full shade. It grows best in gentle, filtered light
    beneath trees and should be protected from strong afternoon sun.
  watering: Keep the soil lightly and consistently moist during active growth. Water
    when the upper layer of soil begins to feel dry, but avoid waterlogged conditions.
    Reduce watering when the plant becomes dormant.
  difficulty: Easy to Moderate
  arScale: 0.15
  flowerImage: {fileID: 0}
